.TH CRABWALL 1 "September 2026" "crabwall 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crabwall \- per-app firewall TUI and CLI for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crabwall
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crabwall
is the user frontend of the crabwall firewall. Without arguments it opens
the live TUI: a connection feed with one-key prompts. The daemon
.BR crabwalld (8)
must be running, otherwise the TUI shows demo data.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "tui [--theme " NAME "] [--icons " plain | nerd "]"
Launch the live TUI (default when no command is given). Themes: phosphor
(default), gruvbox, dracula, nord, tokyo, catppuccin, mono. Also settable
via CRABWALL_THEME / CRABWALL_ICONS.
.TP
.BI "up [--theme " NAME "] [--icons " SET "] [--learn " SECS "] [--default " ask | allow | deny "]"
Start the daemon if needed and open the TUI. One command, one env: both
sides resolve the same socket/rules/db, so paths can never diverge.
Stops its daemon on exit; see
.B down
for orphans.
.TP
.B down
Stop a daemon previously started by
.BR up .
.TP
.B status
Check whether
.B crabwalld
is reachable and print its IPC version and default policy.
.TP
.BI "logs [--limit " N "] [--json]"
Show recent connections from the event log (default 20, newest first).
.TP
.BI "allow --app " APP " [--domain " D "] [--port " P "]"
Append an allow rule.
.TP
.BI "deny --app " APP " [--domain " D "] [--port " P "]"
Append a deny rule.
.TP
.B rules
Print the current rules file.
.TP
.B config [show]
Show effective settings and where each comes from (flag, file, env, default).
.TP
.BI "config set " "theme " id "| icons " plain | nerd
Persist a setting to
.I ~/.config/crabwall/config.toml .
The TUI also saves the theme/icons on exit when changed with
.B t
/
.B i .
.SH "TUI KEYS"
.TP
.B y / Y
Allow once / always (persist to rules file).
.TP
.B n / N
Deny once / always.
.TP
.B s
Allow until daemon restart (session).
.TP
.B Up / Down , j / k
Select connection.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch feed / rules tabs.
.TP
.B t / i
Cycle color theme / toggle plain/nerd icons.
.TP
.B q / Esc
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/crabwall/rules.toml
Firewall rules (TOML). See
.BR crabwalld (8)
for the format.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/crabwall/events.db
SQLite connection log.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRABWALL_SOCK
Unix socket path (default /run/crabwall.sock for root,
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/crabwall.sock otherwise).
.TP
.B CRABWALL_RULES , CRABWALL_DB
Override the rules file and log database paths.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR crabwalld (8)
.SH AUTHORS
crabwall contributors.
